<LegalPage title="Privacy" description="How Flicksy handles local media and purchase data." updated="September 3, 2026">
  <p>Flicksy is a local Mac app. Your media content, media paths, folders, tags, collections, favorites, and other library metadata are not transmitted to Flicksy or stored in a Flicksy account.</p>

  <h2>Direct licenses</h2>
  <p>When you activate, validate, or deactivate a direct license, Flicksy sends the license key and an app-generated installation identifier to Lemon Squeezy, along with the product identifiers needed to verify the purchase. Flicksy does not send your computer name. Checkout and receipt email are handled by Lemon Squeezy; the Flicksy app does not request or store that email.</p>

  <h2>Direct updates</h2>
  <p>The direct app contacts Flicksy’s HTTPS update feed to check for signed updates. Flicksy does not enable Sparkle’s system-profile reporting.</p>

  <h2>Mac App Store</h2>
  <p>The App Store version asks Apple to verify trial and purchase entitlements. Apple’s collection and handling of App Store data is governed by Apple’s policies.</p>
</LegalPage>
